      <details class="faq-item" open>
        <summary>What&#39;s the difference between Owner&#39;s Project Management, Clerk of the Works, and Construction Advisory?</summary>
        <div class="faq-item__body"><p>Owner's Project Management represents you from start to finish: permitting, procurement, design, buy-out and close-out. Clerk of the Works is on-site supervision focused on cost and quality. Construction Advisory doesn't run the job site day to day. It's an independent check on construction risks and technical decisions alongside your owner's rep.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What do you need from me to get started?</summary>
